---
import EntetePage from '~/components/EntetePage.astro';
import FicheLegale from '~/components/FicheLegale.astro';
import site from '~/data/site.json';
import { champ } from '~/i18n/site';
import { chemin } from '~/i18n/config';

const { hebergeur: h, contact: c } = site;
const maj = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-GB', {
  day: 'numeric', month: 'long', year: 'numeric', timeZone: 'Europe/Madrid',
}).format(new Date('2026-09-03'));
---
<EntetePage
  surtitre="Legal information"
  titre="Legal notice"
  chapo="Who publishes this site, who hosts it, and what you may do with it. This is the information required by article 10 of Spanish Law 34/2002 (LSSI-CE)."
  ariane={[{ libelle: 'Legal notice' }]}
  registre="papier"
/>
<section class="section conteneur">
  <div class="prose">

    <h2>1. Publisher</h2>
    <FicheLegale langue="en" />

    <h2>2. Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      This site is hosted by <strong>{h.nom}</strong>, {champ(h.adresse, 'en')}
      {' '}(<a href={h.site} class="lien" rel="noopener">{h.site.replace('https://', '')}</a>),
      through its {h.service} service.
    </p>
    <p>
      It is a static site: pages are generated in advance and served as they are, with no database
      and no processing on the server.
    </p>

    <h2>3. What this site is for</h2>
    <p>
      This site presents the activity of {site.nom}: its gatherings, the people who speak at them,
      its projects and its writing. Access is free and open. Nothing is sold here, there is no
      payment and no commercial transaction.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Terms of use</h2>
    <h3>What you may do</h3>
    <p>
      You may read this site, quote it, share its addresses and reproduce extracts for private,
      educational, community or journalistic use, as long as you credit {site.nom} and do not
      distort the content. For any other use, commercial in particular, write to us: we answer.
    </p>
    <h3>What you may not do</h3>
    <p>
      The following are not allowed: systematic extraction or reuse of a substantial part of the
      content, any attempt at unauthorised access, any action meant to disrupt the running of the
      site, and use of the published contact addresses for unsolicited canvassing.
    </p>
    <h3>Links</h3>
    <p>
      Outgoing links point to sites we do not control and are not answerable for. You may link to
      this site without asking us, as long as the link does not mislead anyone about where the
      content comes from.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The texts published on this site belong to {site.nom} unless stated otherwise. Photographs
      remain the property of their authors: every published image carries its credit where one has
      been given to us. The visual identity and the name {site.nom} belong to the association.
    </p>
    <p>
      Portraits, stories and photographs of people are published with the agreement of the people
      concerned. If you appear in an image or a text and want it taken down, write to us: we do it,
      without argument and without delay.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Liability</h2>
    <p>
      We do our best to publish accurate, up-to-date information, in particular the dates and
      venues of gatherings. An error is still possible: it cannot engage the association’s
      liability. Announced dates and venues may change; the event page is the one that counts.
    </p>
    <p>
      The site is offered as it is. We guarantee neither continuous availability nor the absence of
      interruptions for maintenance or on the host’s side.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Data protection and cookies</h2>
    <p>
      How personal data is handled is set out in the
      {' '}<a href={chemin('en', 'confidentialite')} class="lien">privacy policy</a>. The use of
      cookies and local storage is set out in the
      {' '}<a href={chemin('en', 'cookies')} class="lien">cookie policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Applicable law</h2>
    <p>
      This legal notice is governed by Spanish law, in particular Law 34/2002 on information
      society services and electronic commerce (LSSI-CE). Any dispute falls to the competent courts
      of Barcelona, without prejudice to the protective rules applicable to consumers.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Telling us about something</h2>
    <p>
      An error, content that should not be there, a broken link, an image to take down: write to
      {' '}<a href={`mailto:${c.email}`} class="lien">{c.email}</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="maj">Last updated: {maj}.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .maj { margin-top: var(--e-8); font-size: var(--t-200); color: var(--encre-faible); }
</style>
